Design a circuit that performs a 4-bit unsigned multiplication. The module takes two 4-bit inputs, A and B, and calculates the product, resulting in an 8-bit output. It computes the partial products of A with each bit of B and aggregates these to form the final product, effectively implementing a simple combinatorial multiplier.
