Design a circuit that computes the parity bit for an 8-bit input data. The module takes an 8-bit input, D, and outputs a single bit, P, which reflects the even or odd parity of the input bits. The parity output is toggled based on the number of set bits in the input; if the count of 1s is odd, P will be HIGH, otherwise, it will be LOW.
