description:
Design a dual 1-bit D flip-flop. This module captures the 2-bit input `d` on the rising edge of the clock signal `clk`. It resets the output `q` to 0 asynchronously when the clear signal `clrn` is asserted low (negedge). When `clrn` is high, the output follows the input `d`, effectively storing the input data.
module top_module(d,clk,clrn,q
    );

code:
module top_module(d,clk,clrn,q
    );input [1:0] d;
	 input clk,clrn;
	 output [1:0] q;
    reg [1:0] q;
    always @ (posedge clk or negedge clrn) begin
			if (clrn == 0) q <= 0;
			else				q <= d;
	 end	 
endmodule

