description:
Design a circuit that computes the minimum and maximum values from an n-bit wide input signal, where n is parameterized to specify the number of input bits. The module initializes the minimum and maximum outputs to the first input value and iteratively compares each subsequent input to update the minimum and maximum accordingly. This functionality allows for real-time evaluation of the smallest and largest values within the provided input array.
module top_module(
  input [n-1:0] in,
  output reg [n-1:0] min,
  output reg [n-1:0] max
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [n-1:0] in,
  output reg [n-1:0] min,
  output reg [n-1:0] max
);parameter n = 8; // number of input signals

integer i;

always @(*) begin
  min = in[0];
  max = in[0];
  for (i = 1; i < n; i = i + 1) begin
    if (in[i] < min) begin
      min = in[i];
    end
    if (in[i] > max) begin
      max = in[i];
    end
  end
end

endmodule

